      "text": "To determine which segment is the longest in the given figure, we need to analyze the angles and the lengths of the segments. The segments are labeled as \\(AB\\), \\(BC\\), \\(CD\\), \\(DA\\), and \\(BD\\). The angles given are \\( \\angle BAD = 55^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle BAC = 55^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle ACD = 40^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle CAD = 75^\\circ \\).\n\nFirst, let's find the angles at point \\(C\\):\n- Since \\( \\angle BAC = 55^\\circ \\), and \\( \\angle ACD = 40^\\circ \\), we need to find the angle \\( \\angle BCA \\). The angle \\( \\angle BCA \\) is the external angle to \\( \\triangle ACD \\), so it is \\(180^\\circ - \\angle CAD - \\angle ACD = 180^\\circ - 75^\\circ - 40^\\circ = 65^\\circ \\).\n\nNow, let's use the Law of Sines in \\( \\triangle ACD \\) to find the length of \\(CD\\). The Law of Sines states:\n\\[\n\\frac{CD}{\\sin \\angle CAD} = \\frac{AC}{\\sin \\angle ACD}\n\\]\nSince \\( \\angle CAD = 75^\\circ \\) and \\( \\angle ACD = 40^\\circ \\), we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{CD}{\\sin 75^\\circ} = \\frac{AC}{\\sin 40^\\circ}\n\\]\nHowever, we don't need the exact length of \\(AC\\) to compare the segments. Instead, we can use the fact that the longest segment will be the one opposite the largest angle in the triangle.\n\nNext, let's find the angles at point \\(D\\):\n- Since \\( \\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - \\angle ABD - \\angle BDA \\) and \\( \\angle ABD = 55^\\circ \\), \\( \\angle BDA = 180^\\circ - 55^\\circ - 75^\\circ = 50^\\circ \\). Now, to find \\( \\angle ADB \\), we use the fact that the sum of angles in triangle \\(ABD\\) is \\(180^\\circ\\):\n\\[\n\\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - 55^\\circ - 75^\\circ = 50^\\circ\n\\]\nThis confirms our previous calculation.\n\nNow, let's compare the segments:\n- \\(AB\\) and \\(BD\\) are opposite the angles \\(55^\\circ\\) and \\(50^\\circ\\) respectively.\n- \\(BC\\) is opposite the angle \\(40^\\circ\\).\n- \\(CD\\) is opposite the angle \\(75^\\circ\\).\n- \\(DA\\) is opposite the angle \\(75^\\circ\\).\n\nThe angle \\(75^\\circ\\) is the largest angle in the triangle. Therefore, the segment opposite the angle \\(75^\\circ\\) is the longest. This means \\(CD\\) is the longest segment.\n\nThus, the longest segment is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{CD}\n\\]",
