      "text": "To determine which of the five segments is the longest, we need to analyze the given angles and the lengths of the sides in the figure. Let's denote the segments as follows:\n- \\( AB \\)\n- \\( BC \\)\n- \\( CD \\)\n- \\( DA \\)\n\nWe know the following:\n- \\(\\angle BAC = 55^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle ACD = 55^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle BDC = 40^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle CDA = 75^\\circ\\)\n\nFrom these, we can infer the following relationships:\n- \\(\\angle ADB = 180^\\circ - \\angle BDC = 180^\\circ - 40^\\circ = 140^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle CBA = 180^\\circ - \\angle BAC = 180^\\circ - 55^\\circ = 125^\\circ\\)\n\nNow, let's consider the segments:\n- \\( AB \\) is opposite to \\(\\angle ACD\\) and \\(\\angle CDA\\).\n- \\( CD \\) is opposite to \\(\\angle ABC\\) and \\(\\angle BAC\\).\n- \\( DA \\) is opposite to \\(\\angle ADB\\) and \\(\\angle BDC\\).\n- \\( BC \\) and \\( DA \\) are opposite to the remaining angles.\n\nSince \\(\\angle ACD = 55^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle CDA = 75^\\circ\\), and \\(\\angle ADB = 140^\\circ\\), we can determine the length of segment \\( CD \\) by considering the sum of the angles in triangle \\( ACD \\). The angle opposite \\( CD \\) is \\( \\angle CDA = 75^\\circ \\).\n\nThe length of \\( CD \\) can be maximized if \\( CD \\) is the hypotenuse of the right triangle formed by the angle \\( 75^\\circ \\). The length of \\( CD \\) can be calculated using the Law of Sines in triangle \\( ACD \\):\n\\[\n\\frac{CD}{\\sin 55^\\circ} = \\frac{A}{\\sin 75^\\circ}\n\\]\nwhere \\( A \\) is the length of \\( AC \\). Since \\( \\sin 75^\\circ = \\sin (45^\\circ + 30^\\circ) = \\sin 45^\\circ \\cos 30^\\circ + \\cos 45^\\circ \\sin 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\), we have:\n\\[\nCD = A \\cdot \\frac{\\sin 55^\\circ}{\\sin 75^\\circ} = A \\cdot \\frac{\\sin 55^\\circ}{\\frac{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}{4}} = A \\cdot \\frac{4 \\sin 55^\\circ}{\\sqrt{6} + \\sqrt{2}}\n\\]\n\nSimilarly, we can calculate the length of \\( BC \\) and \\( DA \\), but since \\(\\angle BAC = 55^\\circ\\) and \\(\\angle BDC = 40^\\circ\\), the length of \\( BC \\) will be less than the length of \\( CD \\) because \\(\\angle BDC\\) is less than \\(\\angle BAC\\).\n\nTherefore, the longest segment is \\( CD \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{CD}\n\\]",
